  "question": {
    "text": "If in a triangle $\\mathrm{ABC}$, the altitudes from the vertices $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{C}$ on opposite sides are in H.P., then $\\sin A, \\sin B, \\sin C$ are in",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "SHbnm",
      "text": "\nG.P.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5mI3r",
      "text": "\nA.P.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "QydZp",
      "text": "\nArithmetic - Geometric Progression\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nkreL",
      "text": "\nH.P.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\Delta=\\frac{1}{2} p_1 a=\\frac{1}{2} p_2 b=\\frac{1}{2} p_3 b$\n$p_1, p_2, p_3$ are in H.P.\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{2 \\Delta}{a}, \\frac{2 \\Delta}{b}, \\frac{2 \\Delta}{c}$ are in H.P.\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{a}, \\frac{1}{b}, \\frac{1}{c}$ are in H.P\n$\\Rightarrow a, b, c$ are in A.P.\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin A, \\sin B, \\sin C$ are in A.P.",
    "image": null
